From e3931926e09d952d2eba30c1fe088e19e4fadd30 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Mon, 14 Sep 2026 16:41:03 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Fix what the live site got wrong: hidden forecast, flooded
 news, dead proxy lane

Found by loading the deployed page rather than the local copy.

Forecast panel was invisible below 1080px
- It was display:none behind a toggle most people never find, so on a laptop
  the page showed a chart and no forecast, which is the point of the page.
- Between 760 and 1080 it now sits under the chart as a row of cards instead
  of disappearing. Capped at 34vh so the news console keeps its space.

Nearly half of all headlines were tagged HIGH impact
- impact_high contained bare institution words (rbi, policy, government), so
  "RBI invites comments on draft KYC directions" read as urgent.
- Impact now needs corroboration: a high term plus either a second high term
  or real sentiment. Added a procedural list (invites comments, auction of,
  treasury bills, corrigendum...) that downgrades notices.
- On the live 600-item feed this moves HIGH from 270 to 103.
- Same rule in core.js and fetch_news.py so both lanes still agree.

RBI press releases were flooding the news stream
- That feed posts ~20 notices sharing one timestamp, so it owned the whole
  visible list by recency.
- Display now holds back an over-represented source: max 3 in a row, 12 on
  screen. Nothing is dropped, scoring and the forecast still see everything.
- Distinct sources in the visible 120 goes from a handful to 42.

Removed the browser-side proxied RSS lane
- Measured from the live origin: r.jina.ai rate limits (429) and strips RSS to
  text so no <item> survives, allorigins refused connections, rss2json errored.
- It cost a request per cycle and returned nothing. Breadth is the workflow's
  job, and that had 177 of 183 polled feeds alive on its last run.
- The proxy chain stays for Yahoo candles, where it does work.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
